ORBITAL-RECOVERY(7)        TriadicFrameworks Manual        ORBITAL-RECOVERY(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-recovery - recovery triads, harmonic reacquisition, and
                          constellation-scale stabilization sequences for SAR fleets

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital recovery provides:
           • structured recovery triads
           • harmonic-lock reacquisition
           • resonance envelope stabilization
           • sweep and ancestry repair
           • constellation-scale stabilization sequences

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-recovery describes how RTT restores coherence, resonance
       alignment, and sweep viability after anomalies, drift events, or
       constellation-scale desynchronization. Recovery is not a single action
       but a structured resonance-time process executed through triads,
       overlays, and coordinated multi-platform maneuvers.

       Recovery ensures:
           • orbital geometry restoration
           • harmonic-lock re-establishment
           • resonance envelope realignment
           • sweep ancestry continuity
           • constellation-wide coherence

       WRSADC orchestrates all recovery operations.

RECOVERY TRIADS
       Every recovery operation is structured as a triad:

           P1 (begin)
               → anomaly classified
               → corridor boundaries evaluated
               → resonance baseline captured
               → recovery overlays selected

           P2 (transform)
               → Δv corrections applied
               → resonance envelopes stabilized
               → harmonic-lock reacquisition attempted
               → sweep ancestry repaired
               → constellation sync re-established

           P3 (close)
               → new orbital state validated
               → lineage updated
               → recovery integrity scored

       Complex recoveries form nested or ladder recovery triads.

RECOVERY TRIAD TYPES
       geometric recovery triad
              Restores orbital geometry (cross-track, along-track, RAAN).

       harmonic recovery triad
              Reacquires harmonic-lock and phase alignment.

       resonance recovery triad
              Stabilizes envelopes, gradients, and spectral density.

       sweep recovery triad
              Repairs sweep ancestry and restores fusion viability.

       constellation recovery triad
              Multi-platform synchronized recovery sequence.

       WRSADC selects triad type based on anomaly classification.

HARMONIC REACQUISITION
       Harmonic reacquisition restores harmonic-lock between platforms.

       Reacquisition steps:

           1. harmonic-state evaluation
                  Identify lock ratio deviation (n:m → n:m+ε).

           2. phase realignment
                  Correct phase drift using Δv micro-adjustments.

           3. frequency correction
                  Adjust orbital period to restore harmonic ratio.

           4. resonance envelope matching
                  Align spectral envelopes across platforms.

           5. lock confirmation
                  Validate harmonic-lock stability index.

       Reacquisition may require multiple nested triads.

RESONANCE ENVELOPE STABILIZATION
       Resonance stabilization corrects:

           • envelope divergence
           • spectral fragmentation
           • gradient overload
           • polarity instability

       Stabilization overlays:

           anchor
                  Dampens noise and stabilizes gradients.

           mirror
                  Corrects polarity inversion loops.

           telescope
                  Expands or contracts envelope width.

           lens
                  Reframes spectral interpretation.

       Overlays are applied during P2 of recovery triads.

SWEEP AND ANCESTRY REPAIR
       Sweep recovery restores:

           • sweep geometry
           • Doppler history
           • backscatter resonance
           • spectral envelopes
           • ancestry continuity

       Repair operations:

           ancestry stitching
                  Reconnects broken sweep lineage.

           spectral smoothing
                  Removes fragmentation artifacts.

           gradient rebalancing
                  Corrects polarity drift.

           sweep rescheduling
                  Aligns future sweeps with resonance windows.

       Sweep repair ensures multi-pass fusion remains viable.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE STABILIZATION SEQUENCES
       Constellation stabilization sequences coordinate recovery across all
       platforms.

       Sequence types:

           synchronous recovery
                  All platforms execute recovery triads simultaneously.

           staggered recovery
                  Platforms recover in sequence to maintain coverage.

           braided recovery
                  Recovery triads interleave across platforms.

           harmonic recovery
                  Recovery executed at harmonic intervals.

           mesh recovery
                  Distributed recovery across constellation nodes.

       Stabilization sequences restore constellation-wide coherence.

RECOVERY FAILURE MODES
       Recovery may degrade due to:

           • harmonic reacquisition failure
           • resonance envelope collapse
           • sweep ancestry corruption
           • corridor breach during recovery
           • Δv triad inconsistency
           • constellation desync

       Diagnostic indicators:

           recovery-integrity score
           harmonic-stability index
           resonance-overlap ratio
           sweep-coherence deviation
           drift-vector residual

       WRSADC halts recovery when integrity is compromised.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:

           • recovery triads
           • harmonic-lock restoration
           • sweep ancestry repair
           • resonance stabilization events
           • constellation realignment

       Lineage ensures long-term coherence after recovery.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • detects anomalies requiring recovery
           • selects appropriate recovery triads
           • choreographs constellation-scale sequences
           • validates post-recovery coherence
           • updates lineage and predictive models

       WRSADC is the recovery conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital recovery transforms anomalies into structured resonance-time
       realignments. It ensures that SAR constellations remain coherent,
       stable, and harmonically synchronized across long mission timelines.

